Q2. API Testing with Postman (10 Marks)

Step 1:
Created a Postman Collection named "Product API Collection".

Step 2:
Added the following API requests:
1. GET /products
2. POST /products
3. PUT /products/{id}
4. DELETE /products/{id}

Step 3:
Added a test for successful product creation in the POST request.

Postman Test Script:

pm.test("Status code is 201", function () {
    pm.response.to.have.status(201);
});

pm.test("Product Created Successfully", function () {
    var jsonData = pm.response.json();
    pm.expect(jsonData.message).to.eql("Product Added Successfully");
});

Step 4:
Executed the requests and verified the responses.

Step 5:
Exported the collection using:
Collection → Export → Collection v2.1 JSON Format